--[[
	KitSpec: generated by blender/build_vehicles.py (blender/facadekit.py). Do not edit by hand.

	For every city kit fitted to a stand-in part (PartKit.Kit), the box it was modelled on: the part's
	size in the design city (studs), x along the wall, y up, z into the wall (the front is -z).
	Models/CityKit scales the kit by the part's size over this box. A tiled kit (Tile = the axis whose
	scale sets the module's size) is laid along x as many times as fit, each one kept in proportion.
	A ring kit (a cornice) runs round the part's box, the box its outside: modules along each wall
	(Reference: a module's length, height and projection) and the Corner kit at each corner.
]]

